==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns after 102 seconds<sup>3,060f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 20% HP:
**1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns.
**1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Start the battle by upgrading the [[Worker Cat]]. When the enemies come near the [[Cat Base]], spawn a few meatshields and [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cats]] (2 or more). Upgrade your Worker Cat to max level. You obviously want to test out your newest cat, so sending out [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]] would be a good idea. Support your Fish Cat with meatshields, Axe Cats, and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cats]]. When Hippoe and Pigge spawn, let them progress to your base. When they come close enough, go all-out with meatshields, Axe Cats, Gross Cats and Fish Cats.

